      "body": "Adds public market-data fallback, persistent contract-specific OI history, and verified venue-scoped CVD/executed liquidation observations. The dashboard remains read-only and exchange flows remain unavailable, so both panels stay NO TRADE.\n\nData behavior:\n- Spot/candles/funding/OI use public Coinbase, Kraken and Deribit sources with explicit timestamps, units and provider diagnostics. OI windows remain separate by provider/contract/native units.\n- CVD covers 15 completed minutes on one perpetual contract: Kraken minute buy/sell analytics, falling back to a complete Deribit trade tape in native USD units. Truncated/saturated ranges, sequence gaps, unknown directions or negotiated trades fail closed. No spot sample is promoted to verified CVD.\n- Executed liquidation volume uses Kraken minute analytics, falling back to complete Kraken execution history with bounded paging, coverage boundaries, sequence checks and conflict detection. This is endpoint fallback within Kraken, not independent-provider redundancy. BTC fallback sequence gaps seen live were rejected; ETH fallback validated.\n- Unknown, malformed, non-finite, stale, future or incomplete context inputs remain unavailable. Raw observations are revalidated during assessment; whole windows replace one another without unit conversion or cross-provider splicing.\n\nSafety:\nCVD, liquidation data and exchange flows remain mandatory. Exchange flows have no verified integration and cannot be satisfied by arbitrary flags. Expired, future or changed-input assessments are rejected and source freshness is checked again at signal time. Macro/high-risk gates remain enabled. No estimated liquidation heatmaps, predicted liquidation levels, global coverage claims, trading execution, background collection or alerts.\n\nValidation on 2026-10-10:\n- All 67 unit and Streamlit UI tests passed; git diff --check passed.\n- End-to-end read-only checks exited 0 across eight primary/fallback BTC/ETH scenarios; all sixteen panels returned NO TRADE. Normal scenarios supplied all four OI windows plus verified CVD/liquidation observations.\n- Dedicated context checks exited 0. Actual requests returned HTTP 200; primary outages were simulated and secondary observations were real. Incomplete liquidation secondary coverage was reported as unavailable, never zero.\n- Streamlit emitted upstream NumPy timedelta deprecation warnings without test failures.\n\nCosts/limits:\nImplemented public feeds required no key or subscription. Binance returned regional HTTP 451 and was not enabled. Deribit public real-time liquidation flags are not a reliable zero-activity signal. CoinGlass is a potential keyed paid alternative, not implemented or purchased; advertised plans start at $29/month, with minute history on higher tiers. See docs/context-provider-validation.md for links, entitlement/billing caveats and observed limitations. Point-in-time tests do not establish sustained uptime or a persistence soak.\n\nKeep this PR in draft. No merge, deployment or automated trading enabled.",
